252
00:18:40,926 --> 00:18:44,114
Let's land this. Say each
line in your own words.

253
00:18:44,454 --> 00:18:49,199
The response is contain, assess, eradicate,
recover, communicate, prevent, and the

254
00:18:49,239 --> 00:18:50,949
first step is at the provider.

255
00:18:51,289 --> 00:18:55,649
A deletion adds a commit and removes
nothing; --contains shows every ref that

256
00:18:55,689 --> 00:18:58,850
reaches the adding commit,
including dependent branches.

257
00:18:59,190 --> 00:19:04,395
A rewrite is warranted when the data stays
harmful after rotation or the affected

258
00:19:04,435 --> 00:19:09,446
history is small and unmerged; each
dependent branch is then transplanted with

259
00:19:09,486 --> 00:19:09,899
--onto.

260
00:19:10,239 --> 00:19:14,983
A forced push leaves the objects on the
server and in every clone; they are pruned

261
00:19:15,023 --> 00:19:17,375
per repository, and on GitHub by Support.

262
00:19:17,715 --> 00:19:22,516
"Gone" and "safe" are claimed only after
verification: in every repository for the

263
00:19:22,556 --> 00:19:24,760
